<title>EGYPT: YIELD RISES ON EGYPTIAN 91-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD RISES ON EGYPTIAN 91-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 8.820 percent at Wednesday's auction from 8.800 percent at the previous auction on Aug 6.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 700 million pounds and accepted bids for 768.175 million. Bills worth 1,003.050 million pounds mature.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 11, 1997 (Nov 6, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.820 percent (8.800)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 768.175 million (997.800 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,153.175 million (1.199.800 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.554 - 8.889 percent (8.600 - 8.813)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.554 - 10.099 percent (8.600 - 10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 76 (36)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 86 (47)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
